      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דִּין</span></big>  <strong>substantivo.</strong>[<strong>masculino.</strong>] <strong>juízo</strong>—<a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 17:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.17.8\">Dt 17.8</a> + 16 vezes; com sufixo <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּינִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 9:5\" href=\"/Psalms.9.5\">Sl 9.5</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּינֵךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.13\">Jr 30.13</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">כסא דין</span> <em>trono de juízo</em> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 20:8\" href=\"/Proverbs.20.8\">Pv 20.8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">משׁמים השׁמעת דין</span> <em>desde o céu fizeste ouvir o juízo</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 76:9\" href=\"/Psalms.76.9\">Sl 76.9</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>causa, demanda</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בין דין לדין</span> <em>entre demanda e demanda</em> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 17:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.17.8\">Dt 17.8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דין דין</span> <em>pleitear uma causa</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:28\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.28\">Jr 5.28</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 22:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.22.16\">Jr 22.16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:13\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.13\">Jr 30.13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עשׂה דין</span> <em>defender a causa</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 9:5\" href=\"/Psalms.9.5\">Sl 9.5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 140:13\" href=\"/Psalms.140.13\">Sl 140.13</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ידע דין</span> <em>considerar a causa</em> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 29:7\" href=\"/Proverbs.29.7\">Pv 29.7</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דין לפניו</span> <em>a causa está diante dele</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 35:14\" href=\"/Job.35.14\">Jó 35.14</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שׂנה דין</span> <em>alterar a causa</em> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:5\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.5\">Pv 31.5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">לְהַטּוֹת מִדִּין דַּלִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 10:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.10.2\">Is 10.2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דין יתום</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:28\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.28\">Jr 5.28</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דין כל בני חֲלוֹף</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:8\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.8\">Pv 31.8</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  <em>juízo, condenação</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דין רשׁע</span> <em>juízo do ímpio</em> <a data-ref=\"Job 36:17\" href=\"/Job.36.17\">Jó 36.17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דין ומשׁפט</span> <em>juízo e justiça</em> v. <a data-ref=\"Job 36:17\" href=\"/Job.36.17\">Jó 36.17</a>.<br><strong>4.</strong>  <em>contenda</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דין וקלון</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 22:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.22.10\">Pv 22.10</a> (<em>contenda judicial, litígio</em> Str).<br><strong>5.</strong>  <em>governo</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דת ודין</span> <em>lei e governo</em> <a data-ref=\"Esther 1:13\" href=\"/Esther.1.13\">Et 1.13</a>.<br><em>Nota.</em> —<span dir=\"rtl\">לְמַעַן תֵּדְעוּן שַׁדּיּ֯ן</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 19:29\" href=\"/Job.19.29\">Jó 19.29</a> é explicado de várias maneiras. (1) AV RV <em>para que saibais que há um juízo</em> seguem Aq Symm Theod, assim De Da, interpretando <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ</span> relativo + <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּין</span> <em>juízo</em>, mas <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁ</span> é desconhecido no dialeto de Jó e <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּין</span> é empregado somente na seção de Eliú. (2) 𝔊 lê ὕλη ou ἴσχυς (isto é, <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁדַּי</span> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Job 29:5\" href=\"/Job.29.5\">Jó 29.5</a> 𝔊)? ou <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁד</span>?), e Qere <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁדּוּן</span>, indicando incerteza antiga e um texto corrompido. (3) Ew Di leem <span dir=\"rtl\">שַׁדַּי</span> <em>o Todo-Poderoso</em>, o que está de acordo com o uso de Jó. (4) Siegf <span dir=\"rtl\">כִּי שֻׁדָּ֑דוּ</span> (com dúvida).",
